# Cloudflare Pages custom headers.
#
# ⛔⛔ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS — 2026-08-27.
# The YouTube grid on the home page was fixed, deployed and verified, and The creator still saw the old
# broken message on his screen. The heading had updated but the box under it had not.
# THE CAUSE: index.html revalidates, but `assets/content.js` was served with
#     Cache-Control: public, max-age=14400
# and no version marker in its URL. So a visitor got the NEW html and the OLD javascript, for up to
# four hours. Every future JS fix would have failed to arrive the same silent way.
#
# ⭐ THE FIX IS TWO HALVES AND BOTH ARE REQUIRED:
#   1. Every asset URL now carries ?v=<content hash>, stamped by `stamp_asset_versions.py`.
#      A changed file changes its URL, so a browser cannot serve a stale copy of new code.
#   2. This file: HTML must revalidate every time (it is what carries the new asset URLs), while
#      the versioned assets themselves may be cached hard, because their URL changes when they do.
#
# ⚠️ RUN `python stamp_asset_versions.py` AFTER EDITING ANY FILE IN assets/. If the hash in the
# HTML does not match the file, visitors keep the old one and the deploy looks like it did nothing.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/api/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=900, stale-while-revalidate=86400
